A||||16||87SC/GT||Vette spindles?||||5||
Z||000000||87SC/GT||03-16-2000||09:44 PM||||I recall reading an advertisement for a fiero  based 512TR that stated the 84up Vette spindles/brakes were a bolt in swap for the Fiero aside from the different bolt pattern. Can anyone confirm this? Anyone know of any other similar swaps for large diameter rotors? Thanks, You guys are swell.||||reg||5
Z||000001||william_thorniii||03-16-2000||10:46 PM||||SC/GT,<P>That is an excellent question.  I have heard both the Corvette and Camaro work.  If anyone has any actual information on this subject please let me know as well.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||4
Z||000002||87SC/GT||03-16-2000||11:32 PM||||WT,Don't Camaro's steer from ahead of the "crossmember" ? I suppose you could swap them  side for side but your caliper would be in front. There has to be something out there that is a bolt on deal. What about using rear  disks off a FWD performance car? A bracket to refit a larger caliper to the original spindle would be a piece of cake if I could just find a larger rotor that I could fit to the Fiero spindle. It would be ideal to come up with a large diameter (11-12") swap that could be done as inexpensively as the grand Am swap. Think hard! Think Cheap!||||reg||1
Z||000003||FIEROCIOUS||03-17-2000||12:49 AM||||What about corvette A arms for the front? Rear for that matter? The aluminum kind?||||reg||1
Z||000004||william_thorniii||03-17-2000||08:22 AM||||SC/GT,<P>Yes, the Camaros spindle is completely different.  I was attempting to claim (was the end of a VERY long day for me) that I have heard of the use of Fiero spindles with Camaro disks and calipers.  I also remember a link with a brake upgrade that stated "all parts are from existing GM vehicles".  It couldn't be that hard.  Similar to the GA swap.  If it warms up around here this weekend, I will try to go to the boneyard and do some research.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||2
Z||000005||william_thorniii||03-17-2000||10:38 AM||||SC/GT,<P>I have contacted a VERY reliable source about F and Y-body compatibility.  I still don't know about the actual spindles but at least should find out about the rotors and calipers by Monday.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||14
Z||000006||HarryG||03-17-2000||03:23 PM||||There was an article in PFC about adapting Camaro front calipers and Cadillac rears (keeping e-brake)and using MOPAR rotors which were about 11" diameter, if I recall. This set-up also used the cut-down Fiero front hubs like the Grand Am/Beretta swaps. You need 16" rims for clearance.    ||||reg||1
Z||000007||william_thorniii||03-17-2000||04:44 PM||||Harry,<P>Great information.  Do you know if this article is on-line and if so where I can view it.  Otherwise could you copy and send it to me?  That sounds like the one that I am thinking of.  <P>The 16" wheel thing is not a problem.  I have a nice set of 17"s picked out.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
Z||000008||87SC/GT||03-17-2000||06:38 PM||||WT, That sounds great, I have a set of 17's but no tires. I can send them back if I have to change bolt patterns. 115 x 5 opens up alot of wheel possibilities. 4th gen camaro wheels would be cool! The rear hub/bearing carrier swap is becoming more popular with the kitcar people. I think an inexpensive front swap would answer alot of prayers. The vette swap would be cheaper than the full blown Rayne or wilwood,baer swaps but now we are dealing with a front bolt pattern that is not a likely match for rear upgrades. I recall the vette braked kitcar I saw, used a tornado rear (front in rear). A swap with all GM parts would be the best possible solution. Make it look factory and keep em all guessing! The vette A-arms would look cool but would be tough to do. I looked at an 87 Supra's undercarrige (it was upside down and I got a good look!) and it uses a similar looking suspension to the Vette's but is scaled down. If nothing else, I think I'll nab it for my homebuilt car project. Regards, SC/GT<p>[This message has been edited by 87SC/GT (edited 03-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||lowCG||03-17-2000||07:54 PM||||I'm going to install some Subaru Legacy rotors/BMW calipers soon,total cost is around $500.<BR>Must say that does sound like a great idea though,then get some adapters to make the rear bolt patterns match,and use Vette wheels.Would still need to adapt something for the rear brakes,if it worked.<p>[This message has been edited by lowCG (edited 03-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||william_thorniii||03-17-2000||08:18 PM||||This my friends is hot-rodding in the truest sense of the word!  <P>I'm so very proud of you all.<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||14
Z||000011||batboy||03-17-2000||08:45 PM||||Some of these high dollar big brake kits are merely an adaptor plate they made and a bunch of off the shelf GM parts. For 10.5" rotors and calipers, they often use 86 IROC rear calipers and rotors (with e-brake) and 4 X 4 S-10 pickup front rotors and calipers. You have to still use the front hub setup like a Grand Am swap. If I were to go with bigger calipers, I'd like to use the 4 piston suckers. LowCG, what type are those you're going to use?||||reg||1
Z||000012||william_thorniii||03-17-2000||09:01 PM||||Friends,<P>This article is well written and rather informative.  Check it out:  <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe/99/4/brakes.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe/99/4/brakes.htm</A> <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
Z||000013||william_thorniii||03-17-2000||09:30 PM||||Gentlemen,<P>I really need to get more organized.  After a while of scouring through old messages, I found another message that I have been looking for.  This is from the fiero-list so don't give me too much grief please.. <P>"Date:  Thu, 06 Jan 00 14:46PM EST  <BR>From:  Patrick Szewczyk &lt;pszewc1@uic.edu&gt;    Add To Address Book  Add To Junk Mail Blocker List  <BR>To:  Fiero-list@fiero.org  <BR>Subject:  (Fiero) 11.25 BRAKES WITH HANDBRAKE INTACT = CHEAP     <P>I called V8 Archie up and it turns out that you can use 80's fbody front<BR>brake calipers on the front and back if you don't care to have a parking<BR>brake. The setup uses 11.25" chrysler lebaron vented rotors all around. If<BR>you desire a handbrake then you have to use an early eighties cadillac<BR>seville rear calipers, which are almost the same as the fbodies, but the<BR>cable linkage setup is more compatible. You''ll also need the 4 caliper<BR>brackets, and some cable kit to make it compatible with the fieros system.<BR>This whole setup, he said will only work with the 84-87's. So...<P>full setup prices - approximately:<P>(4) caliper brackets - 220.00 total<BR>(4) lebaron 11.25" vented rotors - about 33.00 each - Trak AUTO<BR>(2) front fbody calipers - 14.99 each after core return - TRAK AUTO<BR>(2) rear caddy calipers - 65.50 each """""""   - TRAK AUTO<BR>(1) cable kit - forgot to ask....probably around 30.00<P>so youre looking at about $ 550.00 he said for 11.25 brakes all around with<BR>a working handbrake. So just get the brackets and cable kit from him, and<BR>hunt for the best prices on all the other stuff. This should work alot<BR>better than the grand am setup I have now that is less than 6 months old.<BR>The grandam setup is way better than the stock setup, but I would like to<BR>do a little racing so I would need a handbrake. Maybe someone with an<BR>automatic would like to buy my setup in spring. It is all new: rotors,<BR>calipers, pads and rotors dont even show wear, and I drive 75 miles a day.<BR>I have a Getrag so I would like to have a handbrake. I won't do this til<BR>spring, after this Chicago winter is over.<P>If anyone wants this setup call him, not me. Good luck. This is much more<BR>cost effective than those overpriced bastards with smaller brakes. <P>1987 Silver GT, 5spd, etc....."<P>Yet another derivation.  <P>William T. Thorn, III<P> <BR>||||reg||3
Z||000014||87SC/GT||03-17-2000||09:31 PM||||Batboy, Now that you mention it,I think I have heard of that swap. I had the Camaro rear caliper in mind. I noticed my father's Caddy has some real nice 4 wheel disks. The caddy may be another good source of parts without all the F-body boys fighting for the parts and driving the prices up. <P>BTW: My father got in a wreck with his Northstar Caddy. I was hoping they would total it so I could start the Northstar GT project. No such luck.||||reg||1
